<title>USA: Commodore revenues off on renovation.</title>
<headline>Commodore revenues off on renovation.</headline>
<dateline>HOLLYWOOD, Fla. 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commodore Holdings Ltd Friday reported a decline in second quarter revenues to $14.2 million from $15.1 million last year, and said it reflects a 24-day period when one of Commodore Cruise Line's vessels, the S.S. Universe Explorer, was out of service while undergoing renovations to comply with SOLAS (Safety Of Life At Sea) fire safety requirements for 1997.</p>
<p>The company said it had earnings per share in the latest quarter of $0.11, up from $0.03 for the same quarter in 1996.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
